American football is extremely popular in the United States, with over 33% of all Americans stating American football is their favorite sport (Beliby 2026). In 2024, the NFL added approximately $29 to $32 billion dollars to the United States economy (California State University, Sacramento 2026).\'a0 At the local level, NFL teams increase local spending by up to 100% on game day (Bank of America Institute 2026).\'a0 Clearly, as the NFL goes, so goes America.\
Given the impact of NFL to the local economy, it is important for both teams and the local government to encourage good NFL governance. The data explored in this paper is vital for NFL teams to decide which players would thrive within the NFL system, the local government who implement fiscal policies to encourage NFL teams to relocate or stay within their jurisdiction, and potential investigations by boffins to identify the underlaying correlation triggers identified in this investigation. Secondary groups impacted by this study includes city planners, architects, and economics who may set financial policy or develop the relevant mathematical models.\
